{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "No route deviation is established under POL-RD-01. The governing measurement is gps_trace.trace_distance_km at 20.35 km against the booked optimal of 20.1 km, an excess of 0.25 km — 1.24% of optimal. POL-RD-01 requires the excess to be greater than 20% of optimal_distance_km AND greater than 0.8 km in absolute terms, both tests passing; 0.25 km fails both, and the platform's own derived deviation status reads 'no deviation'. Where either establishment test fails the clause directs NO_ACTION however the rider characterises the trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00535", "EV-TRIP-00535"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-01 provides that where gps_trace.trace_distance_km and trip_record.actual_distance_km disagree the trace governs, and that the rounded trip-record figure may NOT be cited for the threshold test. Even on the rider's most favourable reading of trip_record.actual_distance_km at 20.4 km, the excess is 0.3 km — still below both the 20% gate and the 0.8 km gate. Neither distance field carries the claim over the threshold.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00535", "EV-GPS-00535"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.thresholds.threshold_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's real grievance is the 67-minute runtime against a 44-minute optimal, and that delay is a traffic event, not a route choice. Traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00535-01 is a HIGH-severity multi-vehicle accident on the SLE northbound near the Lentor exit, recorded as intersecting the route and overlapping the trip window by 60 minutes, with a shortest lawful alternative of 22.8 km. Under POL-RD-03 the justified excess is min(measured excess, 1.30 x (22.8 - 20.1) + 1.00) = min(0.25, 4.51) = 0.25 km, so the entire measured excess sits inside the exoneration cap; the closure-adjusted optimal is 20.35 km and zero excess remains. POL-RD-09(2) adds nothing, because the off-route ERP, toll and surcharge lines on this trip are all SGD 0.00.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00535-01", "EV-GPS-00535", "EV-TRIP-00535", "EV-FARE-00535"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.closure.justified_excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider bears the initial burden under POL-RD-08 and must show, citing evidence IDs, an excess meeting the POL-RD-01 threshold measured from the trace. The claim pleads duration, a missed train and consequential changes; it identifies no distance excess at all, and the artifacts disclose none. An assertion that cites no measurement meeting the threshold carries no weight, and the burden is not discharged.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00535", "EV-TRIP-00535"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"]
    },
    {
      "text": "No repeat-deviation uplift is open to the rider. POL-RD-06 establishes a pattern only where driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 3 or more, or where that figure divided by driver_profile.completed_trips_90d is 0.05 or more with completed_trips_90d of at least 40. EV-DPROF-00535 records deviation_flags_90d = 0 against completed_trips_90d = 250, a ratio of 0.00, and the clause is in any event consulted only where POL-RD-01 records a MATERIAL deviation, which it does not here.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00535"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-RD-01"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The only money a route-deviation dispute moves on a METERED trip is the arithmetic fare differential computed under POL-RD-02, and only after a deviation is established under POL-RD-01. The fare_breakdown shows the trip charged with no refund issued; the recomputed_fare and refund figures in its derived block are mechanical outputs predicated on a deviation being established and do not themselves establish one. The rider's asserted SGD 200 of train changes is a consequential loss for which the fare model carries no line. With no deviation established, the contested amount stands.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00535"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-02"]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Both of you are entitled to know exactly what decided this. The route-deviation policy prices one thing: distance driven beyond the platform's booked optimal route. On this trip the governing trace (EV-GPS-00535: 100% coverage, 403 fixes at a 10-second cadence, no gaps, weight 1.0) measures 20.35 km against the booked optimal of 20.1 km on the trip record (EV-TRIP-00535, weight 1.0). That is an excess of 0.25 km, 1.24% of optimal — and under POL-RD-01 the trace figure governs over the rounded 20.4 km trip-record copy. POL-RD-01 grants a refund only where the excess is BOTH greater than 20% of optimal AND greater than 0.8 km; 0.25 km fails both gates. No deviation is therefore established, and POL-RD-01 directs NO_ACTION however the rider characterises the trip, save for a billing-integrity refund under POL-RD-09(4). Both advocates conceded this threshold, and they are right to have done so.\n\nThat disposes of the fare money. The derived refund figures on EV-FARE-00535 (SGD 6.70 against the booked optimal and SGD 6.35 against the closure-adjusted optimal, on a charged total of SGD 38.66 and a recomputed fare of SGD 31.9950 / SGD 32.32250) are mechanical outputs that presuppose an established deviation; they do not establish one. The rider's conditional request for SGD 6.35/6.70 (POL-RD-02) is answered and rejected on that ground: the condition it depends on never arises.\n\nTo the rider: your real grievance is the 67-minute runtime against the 44-minute estimate, and the train you missed. That is delay, and this policy does not price delay. On a metered fare the time charge (67 min x SGD 0.28 = SGD 18.76) accrues with the time actually spent in the vehicle, and POL-RD-02's recomputation runs only AFTER a distance deviation is established, which it is not. The SGD 30.00 you contested is the consequential cost of the missed connection, not a line of the metered fare, and the fare model carries no head of loss for it — I accept your own concession to that effect, and I cannot award it. The voucher offer is a commercial matter outside this ruling.\n\nTo the driver: you said an accident caused the delay, and the bundle does corroborate you — EV-ADVIS-00535-01 (weight 1.0) is a HIGH-severity LTA DataMall advisory for a multi-vehicle accident on the SLE northbound near the Lentor exit, intersecting the route and overlapping the trip window by 60 minutes. Because no deviation is established there is nothing for POL-RD-03 to exonerate, so I do not need to reach that clause; the measured 0.25 km excess is simply below the POL-RD-01 gates. The clause is likewise not needed for the money: the off-route ERP, toll and surcharge lines on EV-FARE-00535 are all SGD 0.00, so POL-RD-09(2) adds nothing.\n\nNo repeat-deviation uplift (POL-RD-06) is in play: EV-DPROF-00535 records deviation_flags_90d = 0 against completed_trips_90d = 250, and POL-RD-06 is consulted only on a material deviation, which this is not. No phantom gantry or airport-surcharge line exists, so POL-RD-09(4) produces no billing-integrity finding and no referral, and no clause-mandated referral fires. No POL-RD-10 escalation trigger applies: all three artifacts carry trip_id TRP-00535 with matching pickup timestamps, the trace is unimpaired under POL-RD-07(a) to (c) (no gaps, 10-second cadence), every fare line has a counterpart in the trace or trip record, and the evidence is not contradictory. Same-trip and burden limbs of POL-RD-08 are met on both sides, so nothing turns on the burden's allocation.\n\nConfidence is 0.90. Every artifact carrying the deciding facts — the trace, the trip record and the fare breakdown — sits at weight 1.0, well above the 0.70 floor, so no escalation is warranted and the present state of the charge stands.",
    "referrals": []
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

