    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To both parties. This dispute is a ROUTE_DEVIATION claim over trip TRP-00535, charged SGD 38.66 on a METERED fare (EV-FARE-00535). Under POL-RD-01 no money moves on a route-deviation dispute unless the GPS trace shows a distance excess over the booked optimal route.\n\nThe governing measurement is the trace length, gps_trace.trace_distance_km = 20.35 km (EV-GPS-00535), read against the booked optimal route of 20.1 km (EV-TRIP-00535). The excess is 0.25 km, which is 1.24% of optimal. POL-RD-01 establishes a deviation only when the excess is BOTH greater than 20% of the optimal distance (here 4.02 km) AND greater than 0.8 km in absolute terms; both tests must pass, and 0.25 km fails both. The platform's own derived deviation status on the trace reads 'no deviation'. The two advocates agree on this, and so do I. Even on the rounded trip-record figure of 20.4 km, which POL-RD-01 forbids citing for the threshold test, the excess would be 0.3 km and still fail both gates.\n\nBecause no deviation is established, POL-RD-02's fare recomputation never runs. The recomputed-fare and refund figures sitting in the fare breakdown's derived block (SGD 6.35 against the closure-adjusted optimal, SGD 6.70 against the unadjusted one) are mechanical outputs predicated on a deviation being found; they do not themselves establish one, and neither is payable. The metered charge stands as paid: fare_breakdown.payment_status is CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd is 0.00, and POL-GEN-03 directs that state be left as it is.\n\nOn the rider's points. The rider's difficulty is real but it is a delay, not a route defect: 67 minutes driven against a 44-minute platform estimate. The route-deviation policy prices distance and time only through the POL-RD-02 recomputation, which requires an established deviation first. The SGD 30.00 contested, and the SGD 200 of train changes described, are consequential losses for which the fare model carries no line; POL-RD-02 prices only the distance and time lines of the fare breakdown, and no head of loss is provided for a missed connection. The rider's advocate was candid about this and confined the ask to the conditional SGD 6.35; that condition (an excess sufficient under POL-RD-01) is not met, so the figure is not awarded.\n\nOn the driver's points. The driver's assertion of an expressway accident is on file as LTA advisory EV-ADVIS-00535-01 (HIGH severity, SLE northbound near Lentor, overlapping the trip window by 60 minutes, weight 1.0). Exoneration under POL-RD-03 presupposes a deviation to excuse; there is none, so the question is moot and changes nothing. The repeat-deviation check under POL-RD-06 is likewise moot — it is consulted only on a MATERIAL deviation — and in any event EV-DPROF-00535 records deviation_flags_90d = 0 against completed_trips_90d = 250, a ratio of 0.00, well short of the clause's 3-flag or 5% tests, so no driver-conduct referral arises. The driver's contention that an uncited or unsupported traffic assertion does not discharge the burden is not reached, because the advisory is present and the case never leaves POL-RD-01.\n\nOn evidence quality: all artifacts in the bundle sit at weight_multiplier 1.0 and none is flagged. The GPS trace has 100% coverage, 403 fixes at a 10-second cadence, no gaps and a maximum gap of 0 seconds, so it meets none of the impairment limbs (a)-(c) of POL-RD-07 and no POL-RD-10(3) escalation arises. No escalation trigger under POL-RD-10 fires: the trip identifiers all read TRP-00535, the timestamps on trip record, trace and ledger are consistent and run forwards, no exculpatory clause is invoked against a missing artifact, the refund — were one due — is far below SGD 150.00 and below charged_total, the two sides are not in contradiction, and the fare breakdown carries no ERP, toll or surcharge line at all (erp_gantries empty, tolls_erp 0.00, airport_surcharge 0.00), so there is no unmatched charge line and no POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity finding. The minute difference between the fare breakdown's two published payable figures (SGD 6.35 and SGD 6.70) is explained by whether the recomputation uses the closure-adjusted or the booked optimal; neither is owed here.\n\nOutcome: no refund to the rider, no compensation to the driver, and the SGD 38.66 charge stands. The deciding fact — that the driven distance did not exceed the booked optimal by the POL-RD-01 threshold — is carried by the trace (EV-GPS-00535) and the trip record (EV-TRIP-00535), both at weight 1.0, so confidence is capped at 1.0; I have set it at 0.95 to allow for ordinary measurement noise. No referral is made: no clause on these facts produces one.",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

