    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "This is a ROUTE_DEVIATION dispute and the policy that governs it measures distance, so the test is distance, not time.\n\nTo the rider: the fare of SGD 38.66 on EV-FARE-00535 stands. POL-RD-01 requires the excess of actual over optimal distance to be measured from the GPS trace, because where the trace and the rounded trip-record copy disagree the trace governs and the rounded copy may not be cited for the threshold. EV-GPS-00535 records trace_distance_km = 20.35 km against the booked optimal of 20.1 km (EV-TRIP-00535): an excess of 0.25 km, or 1.24%. Both limbs must pass — the excess must be greater than 20% of optimal AND greater than 0.8 km — and 0.25 km fails both. No deviation is therefore established, and the platform's own derived deviation status agrees ('no deviation'). POL-RD-02 only ever recomputes the fare after a deviation is established; the SGD 6.35 (or SGD 6.70) figure in the fare breakdown's derived block is a mechanical output predicated on a deviation being found, so I do not award it. Your SGD 30.00 contested sum, the SGD 200 of changes and the missed train are consequential losses the metered fare model carries no line for, and the 67-minute runtime against the 44-minute estimate is a delay rather than a route deviation — the route-deviation policy does not price it. The SGD 100 voucher offers are outside this ruling.\n\nTo the driver: your traffic explanation is corroborated — EV-ADVIS-00535-01 is a HIGH-severity SLE northbound accident overlapping the trip window by 60 minutes — but the point does not need deciding, because there is no deviation to exonerate and the measured excess (0.25 km) sits inside the POL-RD-03 exoneration cap (min(0.25, 1.30 x (22.8 - 20.1) + 1.00) = 0.25 km) in any event. No billing-integrity defect arises under POL-RD-09(4): every ERP, toll and airport-surcharge line on EV-FARE-00535 is SGD 0.00, and no gantry is charged that the trace does not cross.\n\nOutcome: NO_ACTION. The charge is left as recorded, no refund issues to the rider and no compensation is due to the driver. Confidence 0.90, capped by the weight-1.0 artifacts (EV-GPS-00535 and EV-TRIP-00535) that carry the deciding fact. No referral and no escalation: the trip identifiers match across all three instruments, the trace is complete (100% coverage, 403 fixes, 10-second cadence, no gaps), and no POL-RD-10 trigger fires — in particular the traffic advisory the driver relies on is present in the bundle, so POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
